  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A fire-shrine buried three leagues beneath ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, the Nightshelf colony carved from the Berg's deep tunnels during the Clever Ice Age. The Whispered Shrift~ sits at the colony's architectural heart, though the penguins who pass it on the way to the Lower Galleries give it a wide berth. Its walls bear frost that pulses with a slow, independent rhythm. The ice here remembers corruption spreading like cracks through crystal — impressions consistent with the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, a corruptive practice whose influence radiates outward from ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ itself.
    
    The chamber is small, its walls curving inward at irregular angles. Braziers line them in precise rows, though fewer than half still burn. The floor bears concentric ritual spirals attributed to Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum, worn smooth by successive occupants. On the eastern wall, someone carved an open-jawed orca above the words *'it listens.'* The graffiti is old enough to have partially refrozen into the stone. No one has removed it.
    
    The shrine is also a documented manifestation site for Shawl☽ Sun, the fire-memory magic that allows practitioners to read and burn the Berg's frozen impressions — at the cost of their own. The chronicle "The City that Grew Fat on Fire" records what happened when that practice was pushed past its limits in ☽'slew Nisaemesius~'s lower tunnels. Whether the Shrift was the origin point or merely a surviving node is unclear from the ice.
    
    ## Custody
    
    The Shrift has changed hands three times since the Orca Incursion:
    
    | Period | Holder | Notes |
    |---|---|---|
    | Post-Incursion | ☽'ofund' Guild | The trade-guild held the shrine as territorial claim during their period of deep-tunnel dominance |
    | Faction Wars era | ☽'shadow Covens' Order | Seized during the general collapse of guild authority; the Covens used it as a seat of fire-keeping practice |
    | Present | Unidentified keepers | No faction claims custody; tenders operate without charter or permission |
    
    The current keepers — and no source agrees on who they are — leave offerings at the shrine's center: fire-shards, bone tokens, once a child's carved seal. The offerings are always gone by morning.
    
    ## Hazard Classification
    
    The Shadow Parliament has designated the site ☽-restricted under material hazard classification. Thermal readings register at 18.2 — suspiciously high for this depth — suggesting active fire-core extraction beyond any chartered operation. This detail aligns with the recovery warrant issued for Lovumruius~ Domina, a materially compromised merchant conducting unauthorized extraction in restricted underground territories.
    
    More troubling: ice-memory impressions consistent with sustained Hush☽ Twilight practice — a suppressive technique targeting aurora-light itself — have been measured 1.4 body-lengths below the resting place of Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~, the Nightshelf official whose documented use of the technique caused significant physical degradation. Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ does not remember making those impressions.
    
    The locals call the Shrift 'the Deep Mistake' or 'where we don't go.' They go. They know the route by touch — the particular cold three turns past the Fissure-Gate. They know not to speak their true names inside.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
