  annotation "note_1771588557789_1", anchor: "Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ does not remember making those impressions", text: "In my Crystalline Spiral annotation I stared at a sentence about magic that consumes the studies conducted on it and asked how I would know if the ice had already given me an answer I'd forgotten. Here is the practical case: a Crypt-Chancellor with measurable impressions 1.4 body-lengths below her documented resting place and no memory of producing them. The Spiral does not merely corrupt ice. It corrupts the practitioner's relationship with their own history. The Shrift is not where this principle manifests. It is the proof.", type: :commentary, display: :full
